  "body": "What happens: on main (`4c84fb81` and later, checked at `ee05ba87`) the `camcraft-app` test binary `wire_stamp` does not compile. `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs` (added by PR #1373) builds `WireContourOp` literals without the `taper_deg` field that PR #1163 (wire constant taper, merged as `4c84fb81`) added. The two PRs merged cleanly as text, so GitHub showed both mergeable.\n\nExpected: every test binary of `camcraft-app` compiles on main.\n\nEvidence: two merge-time refresh agents hit it independently (PR #1141 and PR #1181 refreshes, 2026-11-13 ~07:50Z): `wire_stamp` fails to compile on main itself with a missing-field error for `taper_deg`; `git grep taper_deg origin/main -- crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs` finds nothing.\n\nFix shape: add `taper_deg: 0.0` to the `WireContourOp` literals in `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs` (test-only; no product code). Note PR #1181 carries the same edit plus its own `four_axis` field on its branch; whichever merges second takes main's side.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_stamp` compiles and passes on main.\n",
